## QA

Executable flows. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by flow and step number.

plugin-file is on by default (`FilePlugin.meta.profile.key` is in `getDefaults`; see
`packages/apps/composer-app/src/plugin-defs.tsx`).

```mdl
flow QA-1: Upload an image and preview it
  desc: The core file round-trip — upload an inline image via the Create Object form, place it, and read the preview back.
  actors: both
  covers: [F-1.1, F-1.3, F-3.1, F-3.2, T-1, T-4]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - collection: a collection in that space, to create into
    - only the inline BackendDescriptor is registered (default)
    - no File named "qa-image.png" exists — ABORT rather than reusing one this flow did not create
  test:
    - name: Upload the image
      do: In the navtree, click + on a collection and choose File. Drop a small PNG (e.g. 10 KB) named "qa-image.png".
      invoke: |
        org.dxos.operation.file.create {
          file: new File([Uint8Array.from(atob("iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAQAAAC1HAwCAAAAC0lEQVR42mNk+A8AAQUBAScY42YAAAAASUVORK5CYII="), (c) => c.charCodeAt(0))], "qa-image.png", { type: "image/png" }),
          db: $given.space.db
        }
      capture: created
      expect: a File object is created with type "image/png", the given size, and a Blob whose
        data resolves inline
      assert: return $created.object.type === 'image/png' && !!$created.object.data
      note: |
        `file` is a browser `File` object, not a plain literal — the runner constructs it inline
        with `new File(...)` in the invoke snippet rather than passing JSON, since `BrowserFile`
        has no serializable shape.
    - name: Place it in the collection
      do: (the Create Object form places it for you)
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.addObject { object: $created.object, target: $given.collection }
      expect: "qa-image.png" appears as a row under the collection
      assert: |
        return $given.collection.objects.some((ref) => ref.target?.id === $created.object.id);
      note: Coalesced with the previous step — `created.object` is live and cannot cross a snippet boundary.
    - name: Open it and view the preview
      do: Click "qa-image.png" in the navtree.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.appToolkit.open { subject: ["root/$given.space.id/content/collections/$created.object.id"] }
      expect: FileArticle renders an <img> element showing the uploaded image, resolved via a data: URL
      assert: |
        const img = document.querySelector('img[src^="data:"]');
        return !!img && img.complete && img.naturalWidth > 0;
  after:
    - name: Delete the File
      do: Right-click "qa-image.png" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [$created.object], target: $given.collection }
      expect: the row leaves the navtree and its plank closes
```

```mdl
flow QA-2: Reject an oversized or unsupported upload
  desc: The two rejection paths (F-1.4, F-1.5) — a validation round-trip that must leave no ECHO write behind.
  actors: agent
  covers: [F-1.4, F-1.5, T-2, T-3]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - only the inline BackendDescriptor is registered (4 MB cap applies)
  test:
    - name: Reject an unsupported MIME type
      do: In the Create Object form, attempt to upload a .zip file.
      invoke: |
        org.dxos.operation.file.create {
          file: new File([new Uint8Array([80, 75])], "qa.zip", { type: "application/zip" }),
          db: $given.space.db
        }
      expect: the upload is refused with UnsupportedFileTypeError and no File object is created
      assert: |
        return /UnsupportedFileType/.test($error?.message ?? $error?._tag ?? '');
    - name: Reject an oversized file
      do: Attempt to upload a PNG larger than 4 MB.
      invoke: |
        org.dxos.operation.file.create {
          file: new File([new Uint8Array(5 * 1024 * 1024)], "qa-big.png", { type: "image/png" }),
          db: $given.space.db
        }
      expect: the upload is refused with FileTooLargeError and no File object is created
      assert: |
        return /FileTooLarge/.test($error?.message ?? $error?._tag ?? '');
```

